### Usage example

```tsx
<CheckoutPage
  cartItems={[
    { id: '1', name: 'Wireless Headphones', imageUrl: '/img/headphones.jpg', unitPrice: 79.99, quantity: 1 },
    { id: '2', name: 'USB-C Cable', imageUrl: '/img/cable.jpg', unitPrice: 9.99, quantity: 2 },
  ]}
  onBackToCart={() => navigate('/cart')}
  onPay={async (address) => {
    await api.pay(address);
    navigate('/order-confirmation');
  }}
  currency="USD"
/>
```

Notes:
- `onBackToCart` and `onPay` are passed in so this component stays decoupled from your routing/payment logic — wire them to your router and payment API respectively.
- Validation is client-side only; re-validate the address server-side before charging.
- Swap `currency` as needed; prices are formatted via `Intl.NumberFormat`.
